execute every item of the tasklist
- in $route/0.tasklist.md

.why = the tasklist was written 2026-08-30 from a live session's findings. it holds 22 items
across 6 sections, and its order is load-bear: section A settles a name fork that sections
B and C both depend on.

---

## .the order

**A first, and halt on it.** A1 asks whether the family is `grove.provision` (noun-first,
the extant 17 skills) or `provision.grove` (`rule.require.treestruct`'s `[verb][...noun]`).
that answer decides every file B and C rename.

⚠️ **A1 is a fulcrum whose rework is NOT clean** — a wrong guess renames 17 skills plus every
brief, playbook, and howto that names them, and the reverse costs the same again. per
`rule.always.defer-fulcrums-to-last` this is the rare case that earns a halt rather than a
best-guess. surface it, take the human's answer, then drive.

then B → C → D → E → F. within each section the items are independent unless the item says
otherwise.

## .the bar each item must clear

| the item | is done when |
|---|---|
| a rename | every caller found by grep names the new word, and `rhx <new>` runs |
| a delete | **TWO edits** — the file goes, AND every line that named it says what became of it |
| a rule change | the rule's `.enforcement` section states the new bound |
| a new dir | it is gitignored where the tasklist says so, and a brief names its purpose |

## .what to NOT do

- ⛔ do not fold a clamp into `test` without a run of that clamp first. a clamp moved
  unverified is a clamp nobody has seen bite in its new home
  (`gotcha.a-check-that-cries-wolf-gets-silenced`, `.the corollary`)
- ⛔ do not delete a play until its two-question census answer is written down. the readme's
  test is *"does any file CITE it, and is that citation a REACH or a FOOTNOTE?"* — an
  undocumented delete cannot be audited
- ⛔ do not repair E1 (rung 3's self-referential probe) by a guess. it needs a no-tmux box,
  and the infra image ships tmux — so either summon a box that lacks it, or record why the
  item stays open

## .track progress in the yield

after each item, append a row. the yield is the record a reader consults to learn what
became of the tasklist, so a SKIPPED item needs a row as much as a done one.

```md
| item | verdict | what happened |
|---|---|---|
| A1 | ✔ done | human chose `grove.provision`; the extant family stands |
| C2 | ⚠️ partial | 38 exhibits deleted; 4 held — each cited by a REACH, listed below |
| E1 | 🌙 open | needs a no-tmux box; recorded inline at grove.ready.verify.sh |
```

⚠️ a `✔` row owes its EVIDENCE — the command run and what it answered, not a claim that it
was run (`rule.require.trust-but-verify`).

